.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.774,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-90-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2084008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d181f9a9cfe1a9637b379b41673b7bfa6687bdef7d0ff589f9ad8f31aae09239","compact":"2edcd28c1079d554d86c4215754fe788213763f278bd4a45e8984b0a086d5ba8","nasal":"2edcd28c1079d554d86c4215754fe788213763f278bd4a45e8984b0a086d5ba8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-84-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":84,"verse":9,"english":"To all this returning \"So it is,” the illustrious Bharadvāja from affection for Rāghava said to Bharata.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.741,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-90-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2084009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e3157aed8e470cf2c8e84564bbbbca08d697c8b941a979537383044ee3913286","compact":"75c6bd9493146bda48004eb157109f38ca6bff132d11a1221730d226c848d291","nasal":"4e3aa9aa2f21ecb768198ff3f9944314be8c7290be136c3ea07acf0806c7fbdb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-84-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":84,"verse":10,"english":"What is the use of your visit here, seeing that you are engaged in the task of governing the kingdom? Do you relate all this to me; my mind is ill at ease.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-90-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2084010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e34be8557df95d3371a7d1043918055daa887913feac5682498f55d3c02b5b3c","compact":"79dcb2be6ce57311700e863e604b553e6c14ffe1c1a0fd14ea5c38c0e12feeb6","nasal":"79dcb2be6ce57311700e863e604b553e6c14ffe1c1a0fd14ea5c38c0e12feeb6"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-84-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":84,"verse":11,"english":"That slayer of foes and perpetuator of his race who has been born by Kausalyā, and who along with his wife and brother has been banished to the woods for a long term, that illustrious one who enjoined by his sire in the interests of a woman, has become an inhabitant of the woods for fourteen years, do you, desirous of securely enjoying the kingdon belonging to him as well to his younger brother, intend to do any harm to that sinless one?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.866,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-90-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2084011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2369b0f6b452cefdff26d1bb5b54fa5b61c7ad1ee1ee9cd67c60874724366207","compact":"a129798001f44359150a1429db7a374519ff9df5fc10bc3a0a11521656dad204","nasal":"61f8374e4e876009b5d38ed6b6e02f31dc216b59f43d57edde5ef7c7c0c775da"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-84-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":84,"verse":12,"english":"That slayer of foes and perpetuator of his race who has been born by Kausalyā, and who along with his wife and brother has been banished to the woods for a long term, that illustrious one who enjoined by his sire in the interests of a woman, has become an inhabitant of the woods for fourteen years, do you, desirous of securely enjoying the kingdon belonging to him as well to his younger brother, intend to do any harm to that sinless one?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-90-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2084012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5b37cb018844c5c0e9f4b146ee2be1ee4189140c85468407cedad2944cfd5560","compact":"76b2a1bff5e85e859b6d1048c9ec92c6bd018b962e752af01ae3519729f27310","nasal":"76b2a1bff5e85e859b6d1048c9ec92c6bd018b962e752af01ae3519729f27310"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-84-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":84,"verse":13,"e